":"spell_mana_hex.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAABAAAAAQCAYAAAAf8/9hAAAARUlEQVR4nGOcFfPhPwMSuHBuB4OBkQcDNpC2RIARXYyFWIW4ABOxCoexAYxZWiv+Y5NAj4kL53YwTLsWQXTgjoJRQBIAAEt4DyoP6Fm4AAAAAElFTkSuQmCC"}],"animations":[],"description":"# spell_mana_hex\n\nMana hex: a violet ring on the ground, radius 16 u at scale 1; the game expands it outward from the caster to 10 m (356 u, scale about 22).\n\n- Bounds (first set): x -17..17, y 0..1, z -17..17 units (0.97 x 0.02 x 0.97 m). Origin at the base centre, front faces -Z.\n- Texture: 16 x 16, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering; every visible face has its own region painted with its material at world position (identical faces share one). No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: 40.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 35 x 1 x 35 (w x h x d), centred at x 0, z 0\n\n- Glowing cubes (`glow_*`): glow_ring0, glow_ring1, glow_ring10, glow_ring11, glow_ring12, glow_ring13, glow_ring14, glow_ring15, glow_ring16, glow_ring17, glow_ring18, glow_ring19 ...\n\n## Notes\n\n- Bright simple glowing shapes; every lit cube is named `glow_*` (flat colours; the game may scale, spin and fade them). No particles or lights in the file.\n"}